   "answer": "A Current Profile “specifies the Core outcomes that an organization is currently achieving (or attempting to achieve) and characterizes how or to what extent each outcome is being achieved”【2】.  \nA Target Profile “specifies the desired outcomes that an organization has selected and prioritized for achieving its cybersecurity risk management objectives” and reflects anticipated changes such as new requirements, technology adoption, or threat trends【2】.  \n\nIn the AI RMF context the definitions are analogous: a Current Profile indicates how AI is presently managed and the related risks, while a Target Profile indicates the outcomes needed to achieve the desired AI risk‑management goals【3】.",
