   "answer": "RAPTOR first embeds each 100‑token text chunk with SBERT (the multi‑qa‑mpnet‑base‑cos‑v1 encoder) and then applies a clustering algorithm to group chunks whose vector embeddings are similar【2】.  The clustering step organizes the embedded chunks into cohesive groups, using a soft‑clustering approach that allows a node to belong to multiple clusters rather than fixing a single cluster assignment【6】.  These clusters become sibling nodes in the tree, and each parent node stores a summary of its clustered children【4】.",
